      <body>
         <div>
            <head>Translated parts</head>
            <p xml:id="KR1d0052-start">
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-5a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-12T23:58:09.073+09:00">that is the essence of ritual propriety.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-13T00:16:43.48+09:00">                                    5. 13. The course (of duty), virtue, benevolence and righteousness</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-13T03:20:25.569+09:00">polite so as to show up the virtues of ritual propriety</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.29" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-13T03:51:01.764+09:00">Now wild animals have no sense of ritual propriety,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.30" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-13T03:51:07.996+09:00">and so father and son will both go for the same doe. THESE TWO LINES WERE MISSING</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-7a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="chris" modified="2020-03-11T18:55:08.971+09:00">ritual must be studied.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-14a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-17T17:57:44.544+09:00">CH and he will not own private property.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-17a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T17:25:46.077+09:00">CH: When the superior is by the western stairs</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-18a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T17:28:26.109+09:00">                                    7. 31. Outside the curtain or screen (a visitor) should not walk with the formal hasty steps,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T19:26:53.102+09:00">                                    1.2. He carries the (elder's) mat in his arms like the cross-beam of a shadoof.??????</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.29" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T21:14:20.719+09:00">                                    so that the bottom of it may be a cubit from the ground.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.28" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T21:14:16.684+09:00">With his two hands he should hold up his lower garment,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.34" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T21:31:48.233+09:00">LINE MISSING</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.46" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T21:44:23.169+09:00">CH: and refer to the early kings</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.48" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-18T21:51:13.953+09:00">                                    and the teacher puts a question,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-20a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-19T02:44:15.263+09:00">                                    'I wish, when you have a little leisure 閒,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-22a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-19T18:50:35.915+09:00">nor let the lower garment be held up (even) in hot weather.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:30:54.372+09:00">CH: without reference to ritual.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.27" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:32:00.215+09:00">even if he can speak,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-6a.28" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:32:22.735+09:00">                                    does he not have the heart of a brute?</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-8a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:33:13.092+09:00">CH: then their minds are not fearful.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-7a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:33:51.621+09:00">to understand that they are different from beasts.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-7a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:33:55.037+09:00">                                    that is contrary to proprity;</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-9a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:34:57.326+09:00">he will report according the the system of administration therein.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-12a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:38:43.566+09:00">this is the conduct of a filial son.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-13a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:40:05.447+09:00">CH: then the senior person must sit on a separate mat.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:42:08.14+09:00">one should not stand in handing something to somebody sitting.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-19a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:43:20.238+09:00">CH: and one moves the basket with the opening facing oneself.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-23a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T04:45:12.079+09:00">CH: and bowing pick up.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-24a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T05:02:20.499+09:00">Father and son do not share the same mat.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-24a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T05:03:31.982+09:00">                                    having got married, returns home (on a visit),</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-25a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-22T21:02:58.755+09:00">                                    7. 40. When one congratulates (a friend) on his marrying,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-25a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-23T01:12:50.615+09:00">he must avoid befriending him.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-24a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-23T01:23:00.414+09:00">                                    no (male) enters the door of her apartment.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-28a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-10-24T05:33:58.467+09:00">                                    is capped, and receives his appellation.</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_043-1a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="CH" modified="2019-12-13T23:24:03.025+09:00">                                    2. The ancients who wished to illustrate illustrious virtue throughout the kingdom,</seg>
               <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_006-11a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="chris" modified="2020-02-28T16:30:17.59+09:00">nor any extinction of the principles of earth;</seg>
            <seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_001-7a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="chris" modified="2020-03-11T18:55:01.129+09:00">Hence there is the saying,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-5a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2020-04-29T04:37:08.975+09:00">these are what one shares with the common people.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_042-1a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:09:17.883+09:00">If I go throgh this fast</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_042-1a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:09:50.162+09:00">i cannot get to the end of the matter.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_042-1a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:10:25.319+09:00">If I go through all of this that will take time</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_042-1a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:11:41.45+09:00">I won't be finished by the time the guard is changed.(by Harbsmeier,1981)</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_006-50a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:20:29.296+09:00">（The gentleman must）abstain from music and sex（at this time）</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_006-50a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#minmin" modified="2025-09-04T22:20:34.79+09:00">and let none of these come into his presence.——By Harbsmeier,1981</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T17:08:12.197+09:00">In general, the emergence of music</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T00:53:52.616+09:00">originates from the human )stirrings of the mind.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:17:32.535+09:00">and the activation of the human state of mind</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T17:12:39.86+09:00">is brought about by external objects:</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:51:11.967+09:00">affected by external objects one is moved,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:56:03.072+09:00">and so this physically manifests itself in sounds.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:34:36.737+09:00">Sounds respond to these states of mind</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T17:50:52.658+09:00">and they thus produce modulations;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:47:51.931+09:00">when these different modulations constitute an overall pattern</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:21:52.117+09:00">they are called a melody.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:23:33.116+09:00">the juxtaposing of melodies to make a musical performance of these</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T17:54:10.035+09:00">with shields, axes, feathers and plumes,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:24:50.838+09:00">is called music-and-dance-ritual-performance (henceforth music performance).</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T18:06:41.341+09:00">Music performance</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:26:29.094+09:00">is what arises from melodies:</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T23:06:26.812+09:00">its basis is in human stirrings of the mind(affective responses in modern technical parlance), effected by external objects.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:59:59.978+09:00">Thus when a mournful stirring of the mind is effected</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T18:56:50.818+09:00">the sounds produced are uneasy and despondent;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T20:00:05.24+09:00">when a joyful stirring of the mind is effected</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T18:58:59.783+09:00">the sounds produced are calm and easy;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T20:00:24.284+09:00">when a pleased stirring of the mind is effected,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:00:19.602+09:00">the sounds produced are effusive and expansive;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T20:00:41.263+09:00">when an angry stirring of the mind is effected</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:02:19.173+09:00">the sounds produced are harsh and violent;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T00:58:58.204+09:00">when a reverential stirring of the mind is effected</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:10:36.86+09:00">the sounds produced are straightforward and </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T22:21:03.166+09:00">when the loving stirring of the mind is effected,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-03T19:15:25.699+09:00">the sounds produced are balanced and gentle.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T00:59:17.827+09:00">These six stirrings of the mind</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:03:12.72+09:00">are not nature-given features</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:02:32.402+09:00">they are only activated as response to external things.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:19:56.782+09:00">That is why the Former Kings took great care with the means by which they affected the minds (of their subjects).</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:21:37.735+09:00">So ritual was their means to guide their intentions,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:33:12.756+09:00">musical performance was the means to bring harmony to their voicess&gt;(outward) expressions,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T01:35:07.27+09:00">administration was the means to coordinate their actions,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T16:50:41.243+09:00">and punishment was the means to guard against wickedness.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T16:51:55.245+09:00">Ritual propriety, music, punishment and governance</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T16:54:30.014+09:00">ultimately serve the same purpose:</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T16:57:25.773+09:00">they are designed to unify the people's mindsets and bring about the Way of good government.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:09:54.631+09:00">As a matter of principle, melodies</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:10:08.218+09:00">arise in the human mind:</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:10:54.956+09:00">emotions are activated within</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:12:23.663+09:00">and on this basis take shape in sound.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:21:22.121+09:00">When that sound constitutes an aesthetic whole</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:21:43.106+09:00">it is called a melody.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:22:49.571+09:00">Thus it is </seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:29:34.298+09:00">that in a well-ordered age the melodies are calm and joyful,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:30:18.718+09:00">and governance, then, is well-balanced;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:33:15.701+09:00">the melodies from a disorganised age are resentful and angry</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:34:52.339+09:00">and governance, then, is conflict-ridden;</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.53" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:35:33.602+09:00">the melodies of a doomed state are mournful and wistful,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.54" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:36:39.646+09:00">and, there, the people are troubled.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.55" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:43:29.551+09:00">The ways of sounds/tones and melodies/airs</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.56" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-04T17:44:30.558+09:00">are pervasively homogeneous with (the prevailing) governance.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.57" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:36:36.717+09:00">Let C stand stand for the ruler,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.58" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:37:31.861+09:00">let D stand for the ministers,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:39:04.828+09:00">let E stand for the people,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:39:32.444+09:00">let F stand for undertakings,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:39:40.331+09:00">let G stand for things:</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:56:54.841+09:00">when there is no discordance among these five things [1. they are all well-tuned; 2. they are play harmoniously together.]</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:53:25.713+09:00">there will be no caccophonic melodies.</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T18:57:29.959+09:00">When the A is dicordant there is wildness,</seg><seg corresp="#KR1d0052_tls_019-1a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-05T19:06:43.329+09:00">when the </seg></p>
         </div>
      </body>
